    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: default `registrationDate` to the server's current date\n\nThe feature lives on `POST /api/owners`, read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, both wired through OfficeFloor function pipelines.\n\n**API schema** \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`: added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is `allOf OwnerFields`, the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response) both get a `java.time.LocalDate registrationDate`, which Jackson serializes/deserializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n**Entity** \u2014 `Owner.java`: added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it in both directions (name + type match), so no mapper changes were needed.\n\n**Default logic** \u2014 new `ApplyRegistrationDate` function that, when the built owner has no registration date, sets it to `LocalDate.now()`. Wired into `owners.POST.yml` as a governed step between `build` and `save`, following the `Apply<E>` mutate-in-place convention. A supplied date flows through untouched.\n\n**Database schema** \u2014 added `registration_date DATE` to the `owners` table in all four schemas (hsqldb \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres). I also fixed the positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)` seed rows in `hsqldb/data.sql` and `mysql/data.sql` to include the new trailing column (h2/postgres already use explicit column lists).\n\n**Tests**: `AcceptanceTest.coreDefaultsToToday` (omitted date \u2192 today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (supplied `2020-06-15` preserved) both pass; full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
